      "Ornithine transcarbamylase (OTC) deficiency is the most common urea cycle disorder, inherited in an X-linked recessive pattern.",
      "It results from mutations in the OTC gene on the X chromosome, leading to impaired conversion of ornithine and carbamoyl phosphate to citrulline.",
      "Symptoms include hyperammonemia, vomiting, lethargy, and seizures, often presenting in infancy or early childhood.",
      "Diagnosis is confirmed by elevated blood ammonia levels and low citrulline levels, with high orotic acid in urine.",
      "OTC deficiency can lead to encephalopathy and coma if untreated, due to ammonia toxicity.",
      "Classic association with respiratory alkalosis due to hyperventilation from ammonia accumulation.",
      "Management includes dietary protein restriction and ammonia-scavenging drugs like sodium benzoate."
