    "highYield": [
      "Fabry disease is an X-linked recessive lysosomal storage disorder caused by deficiency of alpha-galactosidase A.",
      "It results from mutations in the GLA gene, leading to accumulation of globotriaosylceramide (Gb3) in various tissues.",
      "Symptoms include angiokeratomas, acroparesthesias, hypohidrosis, and corneal verticillata, often appearing in childhood.",
      "Progressive renal failure, cardiac hypertrophy, and cerebrovascular complications occur in adulthood.",
      "Diagnosis is confirmed by reduced alpha-galactosidase A activity in leukocytes or genetic testing for GLA mutations.",
      "Classic association with 'Fabry crisis' - severe pain episodes due to Gb3 accumulation in nerves.",
      "Enzyme replacement therapy with agalsidase beta is available and can reduce symptoms and slow disease progression."
    ],
