      "Löfgren's syndrome is an acute form of sarcoidosis with fever, erythema nodosum, and bilateral hilar lymphadenopathy.",
      "ACE levels are elevated in about 60% of sarcoidosis patients, but not specific.",
      "Pulmonary function tests often show a restrictive pattern."
