      "Villous atrophy and crypt hyperplasia are characteristic histological findings in the small intestine.",
      "Symptoms include chronic diarrhea, weight loss, and iron deficiency anemia due to malabsorption.",
      "Tissue transglutaminase IgA antibodies are highly sensitive and specific for diagnosis.",
      "Dermatitis herpetiformis is a cutaneous manifestation, presenting as itchy, blistering skin rash.",
      "Increased risk of small bowel lymphoma is associated with untreated celiac disease.",
      "A gluten-free diet is the cornerstone of management, leading to symptom resolution and intestinal healing."
