      "The cardinal signs of acute inflammation are redness, heat, swelling, pain, and loss of function.",
      "Chemical mediators like histamine, prostaglandins, and cytokines play key roles in the inflammatory response.",
      "Histamine causes vasodilation and increased vascular permeability, leading to edema.",
      "Resolution of acute inflammation involves clearance of the inciting stimulus and repair of tissue damage."
