      "Non-human primates are used for more complex studies, such as in neuroscience and infectious diseases, due to their closer physiological and genetic resemblance to humans.",
      "The 3Rs principle (Replacement, Reduction, Refinement) guides ethical use of animals in research.",
      "Knockout mice, where specific genes are inactivated, help in understanding gene function and disease mechanisms.",
      "Transgenic animals have foreign genes inserted into their genome, useful for studying gene expression and regulation."
