      "Normal serum calcium levels range from 8.5 to 10.2 mg/dL.",
      "Hypocalcemia can cause tetany and is often associated with hypoparathyroidism or vitamin D deficiency.",
      "Hypercalcemia is commonly due to hyperparathyroidism or malignancy, presenting with 'stones, bones, groans, and psychiatric overtones'.",
      "Bisphosphonates, like alendronate, inhibit bone resorption by osteoclasts, used in osteoporosis."
