      "The hypothalamus acts as the body's thermostat, regulating core temperature around 37°C.",
      "Heat is lost through radiation, conduction, convection, and evaporation, with evaporation being the most effective in high temperatures.",
      "Shivering thermogenesis increases heat production by up to 5-fold through involuntary muscle contractions.",
      "Non-shivering thermogenesis involves brown adipose tissue and is mediated by norepinephrine.",
      "Sweat glands are activated by sympathetic cholinergic fibers, releasing hypotonic sweat to cool the body.",
      "Fever is a regulated increase in body temperature due to pyrogens affecting the hypothalamic set point.",
      "Heat stroke is characterized by a core temperature above 40°C, CNS dysfunction, and anhidrosis."
