      "Ghrelin, secreted by the stomach, stimulates hunger and increases food intake.",
      "Insulin, in addition to its metabolic effects, also acts on the brain to suppress appetite.",
      "Peptide YY (PYY), released by the gut postprandially, reduces appetite by inhibiting neuropeptide Y (NPY) neurons.",
      "The arcuate nucleus of the hypothalamus is a critical center for integrating hunger and satiety signals.",
      "Mutations in the leptin gene or its receptor can lead to severe obesity due to unregulated appetite.",
      "Bariatric surgery can alter gut hormone levels, contributing to weight loss by reducing hunger."
