      "Cushing's disease is characterized by ACTH-secreting pituitary adenomas causing excess cortisol production.",
      "Adrenal insufficiency results from inadequate cortisol production, presenting with fatigue, weight loss, and hypotension.",
      "The ACTH stimulation test helps diagnose adrenal insufficiency by assessing cortisol response to synthetic ACTH.",
      "In Addison's disease, both cortisol and aldosterone are deficient, requiring replacement therapy."
