      "The sphenoid sinus is located within the body of the sphenoid bone and drains into the nasal cavity.",
      "The optic canal, located in the lesser wing, transmits the optic nerve (CN II) and ophthalmic artery.",
      "Lesions of the sphenoid bone can affect cranial nerves passing through the superior orbital fissure, such as CN III, IV, V1, and VI.",
      "The foramen ovale and foramen rotundum are located in the sphenoid bone, transmitting branches of the trigeminal nerve."
