      "Key epigenetic mechanisms include DNA methylation, histone modification, and non-coding RNA.",
      "DNA methylation typically represses gene expression and is crucial for X-chromosome inactivation.",
      "Histone acetylation generally promotes gene expression by relaxing chromatin structure.",
      "Non-coding RNAs, such as miRNAs, play roles in post-transcriptional regulation.",
      "Epigenetic changes are reversible and can be influenced by environmental factors.",
      "Aberrant epigenetic regulation is implicated in cancer and developmental disorders."
