        "stem": "A 16-year-old boy presents with recurrent episodes of facial and abdominal swelling without urticaria. Laboratory tests show low C4 levels. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Allergic angioedema"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Hereditary angioedema"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "Anaphylaxis"
          },
          {
            "id": "d",
            "text": "Urticaria"
          }
        ],
        "answerId": "b",
        "explanation": "The absence of urticaria and low C4 levels suggest hereditary angioedema due to C1-INH deficiency.",
