      "Meyer's loop lesions cause superior quadrantanopia ('pie in the sky' defect).",
      "The primary visual cortex processes visual information from the contralateral visual field.",
      "Macular sparing is often seen in occipital lobe lesions due to dual blood supply.",
      "Anterior ischemic optic neuropathy presents with sudden vision loss and a pale optic disc."
