    "highYield": [
      "Trigeminal Neuralgia is characterized by sudden, severe, unilateral facial pain along the distribution of the trigeminal nerve.",
      "The pain is often described as electric shock-like and can be triggered by activities such as chewing or touching the face.",
      "Carbamazepine is the first-line treatment for Trigeminal Neuralgia.",
      "Secondary causes include multiple sclerosis and cerebellopontine angle tumors.",
      "Microvascular decompression is a surgical option for refractory cases.",
      "The condition is more common in women and typically presents after age 50.",
      "MRI is used to rule out secondary causes like tumors or demyelination."
    ],
