    "highYield": [
      "Neurofibromatosis type 1 (NF1) is an autosomal dominant disorder caused by mutations in the NF1 gene on chromosome 17.",
      "Café-au-lait spots are often the earliest manifestation, typically appearing in early childhood.",
      "Lisch nodules, benign iris hamartomas, are present in over 90% of adults with NF1.",
      "Neurofibromas are benign peripheral nerve sheath tumors that can be cutaneous, subcutaneous, or plexiform.",
      "Skeletal abnormalities, such as scoliosis and tibial dysplasia, are common in NF1.",
      "Optic pathway gliomas occur in approximately 15% of patients with NF1, often presenting with vision loss.",
      "The NF1 gene encodes neurofibromin, a tumor suppressor that regulates Ras signaling."
    ],
