      "Spastic CP is the most common type, accounting for approximately 70-80% of cases.",
      "Periventricular leukomalacia is a common cause of spastic diplegia, particularly in premature infants.",
      "Dyskinetic CP is characterized by involuntary movements, often due to basal ganglia damage.",
      "Ataxic CP results from cerebellar damage and is the least common form.",
      "Early signs of CP include delayed motor milestones and abnormal muscle tone.",
      "Management focuses on improving function, which may involve physical therapy, medications, and surgical interventions."
