    "highYield": [
      "Cystic fibrosis (CF) is an autosomal recessive disorder caused by mutations in the CFTR gene, most commonly ΔF508.",
      "CFTR mutations lead to defective chloride channels, resulting in thick, viscous secretions in multiple organs.",
      "Pulmonary manifestations include chronic cough, recurrent infections, and bronchiectasis.",
      "Pancreatic insufficiency is common, leading to malabsorption and failure to thrive.",
      "Sweat chloride test is the gold standard for diagnosis, with levels > 60 mmol/L indicating CF.",
      "Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a common pathogen in CF lung infections, often leading to chronic colonization.",
      "Newer therapies like CFTR modulators (e.g., ivacaftor) target specific mutations to improve CFTR function."
    ],
