      "Peak incidence occurs between 2 to 6 months of age, especially in winter months.",
      "Presents with wheezing, cough, and respiratory distress following upper respiratory tract infection.",
      "Chest X-ray may show hyperinflation and atelectasis, but findings are often non-specific.",
      "Supportive care, including oxygen and hydration, is the mainstay of treatment; bronchodilators are not routinely recommended.",
      "Palivizumab is used prophylactically in high-risk infants to prevent RSV infection.",
      "Risk factors include prematurity, congenital heart disease, and chronic lung disease."
