    "highYield": [
      "Pleurodesis is performed to obliterate the pleural space, preventing recurrent pleural effusions or pneumothorax.",
      "Common indications include malignant pleural effusions and recurrent spontaneous pneumothorax.",
      "Chemical pleurodesis involves agents like talc, doxycycline, or bleomycin, with talc being the most effective.",
      "Talc pleurodesis has a success rate of approximately 90% for malignant effusions.",
      "Mechanical pleurodesis involves abrasion of the pleura during thoracoscopy.",
      "Complications of pleurodesis include fever, pain, and acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS).",
      "Contraindications include trapped lung and inability to fully expand the lung."
    ],
