    "highYield": [
      "Bronchopulmonary dysplasia (BPD) is a chronic lung disease primarily affecting premature infants who received oxygen and mechanical ventilation.",
      "It is characterized by inflammation and scarring in the lungs, leading to impaired alveolar development.",
      "Risk factors include prematurity, low birth weight, and prolonged mechanical ventilation.",
      "Diagnosis is clinical, based on the need for supplemental oxygen at 36 weeks postmenstrual age.",
      "BPD is associated with long-term respiratory and neurodevelopmental complications.",
      "Management includes optimizing nutrition, minimizing oxygen toxicity, and using diuretics and bronchodilators.",
      "Corticosteroids may be used to reduce inflammation, but their use is controversial due to potential adverse effects."
    ],
