    "highYield": [
      "Hypersensitivity pneumonitis (HP) is an immune-mediated lung disease caused by inhalation of organic antigens.",
      "Acute HP presents with flu-like symptoms and resolves after antigen removal, while chronic HP leads to fibrosis and irreversible lung damage.",
      "Common antigens include bird droppings, mold, and agricultural dusts.",
      "Diagnosis involves history of exposure, clinical presentation, and imaging findings such as ground-glass opacities on CT.",
      "Lung biopsy may show non-caseating granulomas, lymphocytic infiltrates, and fibrosis in chronic cases.",
      "Management includes antigen avoidance and corticosteroids for severe or chronic cases.",
      "Prognosis is favorable if diagnosed early and exposure is minimized, but chronic HP can lead to pulmonary fibrosis."
    ],
