      "Normal blood pH is tightly regulated between 7.35 and 7.45.",
      "Type A intercalated cells in the collecting duct secrete hydrogen ions and reabsorb bicarbonate.",
      "Ammonium excretion is a key mechanism for renal acid excretion.",
      "Metabolic acidosis can result from increased acid production or decreased bicarbonate reabsorption.",
      "The anion gap helps differentiate causes of metabolic acidosis."
