      "Gitelman syndrome results from mutations in the SLC12A3 gene, affecting the thiazide-sensitive Na-Cl cotransporter.",
      "Both syndromes are autosomal recessive and present with salt wasting and polyuria.",
      "Bartter syndrome can present with hypercalciuria, unlike Gitelman syndrome which has hypocalciuria.",
      "Gitelman syndrome often presents later in life compared to Bartter syndrome."
