      "High-turnover bone disease is due to increased PTH levels, leading to osteitis fibrosa cystica.",
      "Low-turnover bone disease, or adynamic bone disease, occurs with excessive suppression of PTH.",
      "Vitamin D deficiency in CKD leads to decreased intestinal calcium absorption.",
      "Hyperphosphatemia in CKD contributes to secondary hyperparathyroidism.",
      "Aluminum toxicity from dialysis can exacerbate bone disease."
