    "highYield": [
      "Fanconi syndrome involves generalized proximal tubular dysfunction, leading to glucosuria, phosphaturia, and aminoaciduria.",
      "Liddle syndrome is a rare autosomal dominant disorder causing hypertension due to increased sodium reabsorption.",
      "Bartter syndrome affects the thick ascending limb, causing hypokalemic metabolic alkalosis and hypercalciuria.",
      "Gitelman syndrome affects the distal convoluted tubule, leading to hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia, and hypocalciuria.",
      "Fanconi syndrome can be acquired due to drugs like tenofovir or inherited as part of cystinosis.",
      "Liddle syndrome results from mutations in the ENaC channel, leading to increased sodium reabsorption and volume expansion.",
      "Treatment of Liddle syndrome involves amiloride or triamterene, which block ENaC channels."
    ],
