        "answerId": "a",
        "explanation": "Type 3 RTA presents with hyperchloremic metabolic acidosis due to impaired bicarbonate reabsorption and hydrogen ion secretion. High anion gap acidosis is not characteristic of RTA.",
        "tests": "investigation"
