      "Gitelman syndrome is an autosomal recessive disorder characterized by hypokalemic metabolic alkalosis, hypomagnesemia, and hypocalciuria.",
      "It is caused by mutations in the SLC12A3 gene, which encodes the thiazide-sensitive sodium-chloride cotransporter in the distal convoluted tubule.",
      "Patients often present with muscle cramps, fatigue, and tetany due to electrolyte imbalances.",
      "Unlike Bartter syndrome, Gitelman syndrome is associated with hypocalciuria and hypomagnesemia.",
      "The condition typically presents later in childhood or adolescence compared to Bartter syndrome.",
      "Patients have normal to low blood pressure due to renal salt wasting.",
      "Magnesium and potassium supplementation are key components of treatment."
