    "highYield": [
      "Phosphofructokinase-1 (PFK-1) is the rate-limiting enzyme of glycolysis, activated by AMP and fructose-2,6-bisphosphate, inhibited by ATP and citrate.",
      "Fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase is the rate-limiting step of gluconeogenesis, inhibited by AMP and fructose-2,6-bisphosphate.",
      "The bifunctional enzyme PFK-2/FBPase-2 regulates the levels of fructose-2,6-bisphosphate, a key regulator of glycolysis and gluconeogenesis.",
      "Insulin stimulates glycolysis by activating PFK-2, increasing fructose-2,6-bisphosphate, while glucagon has the opposite effect.",
      "Pyruvate kinase is another key glycolytic enzyme, activated by fructose-1,6-bisphosphate and inhibited by ATP and alanine.",
      "Cori cycle involves lactate produced by anaerobic glycolysis in muscles being converted back to glucose in the liver.",
      "Hepatic gluconeogenesis is essential during fasting and is primarily fueled by amino acids, lactate, and glycerol."
    ],
