      "Hantavirus is transmitted via rodent excreta, causing Hantavirus Pulmonary Syndrome (HPS) with high mortality.",
      "Rabies presents with hydrophobia, aerophobia, and progressive paralysis.",
      "Hantavirus infection begins with flu-like symptoms, progressing to acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS).",
      "Rabies diagnosis involves detection of Negri bodies in brain tissue or PCR from saliva/CSF.",
      "Post-exposure prophylaxis for rabies includes wound cleaning, rabies immunoglobulin, and vaccination."
