    "highYield": [
      "Onchocerciasis, or river blindness, is caused by Onchocerca volvulus, transmitted by blackfly bites near fast-flowing rivers.",
      "Chronic infection leads to skin changes, severe itching, and visual impairment due to microfilariae in the skin and eyes.",
      "Diagnosis is confirmed by skin snips showing microfilariae or serology for O. volvulus antibodies.",
      "Ivermectin is the primary treatment, administered every 6 months to reduce microfilarial load.",
      "Doxycycline targets Wolbachia endosymbionts, reducing adult worm viability.",
      "Nodulectomy can be performed to remove palpable nodules containing adult worms.",
      "Vector control through larvicides and community education is essential in endemic areas."
    ],
