      "The disease is characterized by the emergence of a painful blister, typically on the lower limbs, after about a year of infection.",
      "The female worm can grow up to 1 meter long and emerges slowly from the skin, often causing secondary bacterial infections.",
      "Diagnosis is primarily clinical, based on the appearance of the blister and worm emergence.",
      "Control efforts focus on providing clean drinking water and educating communities about filtering water to remove copepods."
