    "id": "add-handling-missing-data-in-research",
    "title": "Handling Missing Data in Research",
    "system": "research",
    "source": "Additional Topics — ERS-1",
    "updated": "2026-07-11",
    "tags": [
      {
        "kind": "system",
        "label": "Essential Research Skill"
      },
      {
        "kind": "lecture",
        "label": "Additional Topic"
      },
      {
        "kind": "mechanism",
        "label": "Missing data"
      }
    ],
    "highYield": [
      "Missing data can introduce bias and reduce the power of a study.",
      "Types of missing data include MCAR (Missing Completely at Random), MAR (Missing at Random), and MNAR (Missing Not at Random).",
      "Listwise deletion removes all data for a case that has any missing values, potentially reducing sample size.",
      "Imputation methods, such as mean imputation or multiple imputation, are used to estimate missing values.",
      "Multiple imputation involves creating several complete datasets and combining results for analysis.",
      "Sensitivity analysis assesses how different methods of handling missing data affect results.",
      "The Little's MCAR test can be used to assess if data is missing completely at random."
    ],
