    "highYield": [
      "Qualitative research focuses on understanding human experiences and social phenomena, often using interviews, focus groups, and thematic analysis.",
      "Common qualitative methodologies include phenomenology, grounded theory, ethnography, and narrative research.",
      "Data collection methods often involve open-ended questions to explore participants' perspectives in depth.",
      "Thematic analysis involves identifying, analyzing, and reporting patterns (themes) within qualitative data.",
      "Triangulation enhances the credibility of qualitative research by using multiple data sources, investigators, or methods.",
      "Saturation is reached when no new information or themes are observed in the data, indicating sufficient data collection.",
      "Reflexivity involves researchers reflecting on their own biases and how these might affect the research process."
    ],
