    "highYield": [
      "Informed consent is a fundamental ethical requirement in clinical trials, ensuring participants understand the risks and benefits.",
      "The Declaration of Helsinki provides ethical guidelines for medical research involving human subjects.",
      "Clinical trials must undergo ethical review by an Institutional Review Board (IRB) or Ethics Committee before initiation.",
      "The principle of beneficence requires that the potential benefits of a trial outweigh the risks to participants.",
      "Randomization and blinding help reduce bias and ensure the scientific validity of trial results.",
      "Vulnerable populations, such as children and prisoners, require additional protections in clinical research.",
      "Adverse event monitoring is essential to ensure participant safety throughout the trial."
    ],
